      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Leucine acts as a key amino acid sensor by directly activating the Rag GTPases, which then recruit and activate mTORC1. This activation initiates a cascade of signaling events that promote protein synthesis within the cell. Regarding caloric surplus, it provides the necessary energy substrate to support the heightened anabolic demands of muscle building. By exceeding maintenance energy needs, a surplus allows the body to convert excess nutrients into muscle tissue, positively impacting nitrogen balance to favor net protein accretion for hypertrophy.",
      "source": "target",
