      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If the caloric surplus is insufficient, the cell lacks the necessary ATP and energy intermediates required to fuel the energetically expensive process of muscle protein synthesis, overriding the leucine signal. Moreover, insufficient nutrient timing means leucine arrives when the mTOR pathway is already downregulated from previous activity, leading to suboptimal signaling efficiency. Without adequate overall fuel, even a strong leucine \"on\" signal cannot overcome the systemic energy limitations, resulting in poor nitrogen retention and anabolism.",
      "source": "target",
